@startuml

title Pictureframe - Playback Sequence

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 18

actor "systemd" as Systemd
participant "run-playback.sh" as Playback
participant "sync-media.sh" as Sync
participant "prepare-media.sh" as Prepare
participant "create-playlist.sh" as Playlist
participant "HDMI Display" as Display
participant "Background Audio\nController" as Audio
participant "mpv" as Mpv

note over Systemd, Playback
    The playback service starts the initialization
    sequence before launching mpv.
end note

== Initialization ==

Systemd -> Playback: Start playback service
activate Playback

note right of Playback
    Load configuration
    from pictureframe.env.
end note

== Media synchronization and preparation ==

Playback -> Sync: Synchronize media
Sync --> Playback: Synchronization completed

alt New or changed media available
    Playback -> Prepare: Prepare changed media
    Prepare --> Playback: Preparation completed
else No changes
    note over Playback
        Skip media preparation.
    end note
end

== Playlist generation ==

Playback -> Playlist: Generate playlist
Playlist --> Playback: Playlist generated

break Playlist is empty
    Playback --> Systemd: Exit with error
end

== Display initialization ==

Playback -> Display: Send HDMI-CEC wake request
Playback -> Display: Wait for HDMI connection
Display --> Playback: HDMI connected

== Playback ==

Playback -> Audio: Set idle state

Playback -> Mpv: exec mpv with playlist\nand Lua extensions
deactivate Playback
activate Mpv

note over Playback, Mpv
    exec replaces the Bash process
    with the mpv process.
end note

loop Continuous shuffled playback
    Mpv -> Display: Display image or video

    note right of Mpv
        Lua extensions:
        - Location overlay
        - Background audio coordination
    end note
end

@enduml